---
// Article for the Cursive page (en). Written by hand; the tool above it comes from CursivePage.
import CursivePage from '../components/CursivePage.astro';
---

<CursivePage lang="en">
  <article class="wrap max-w-[900px] mx-auto py-10 text-text">
    <!-- Intro -->
    <header class="text-center mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-[clamp(1.6rem,3.4vw,2.2rem)] font-bold mb-4">Copy and Paste Cursive Alphabets</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.8] mb-3">Cursive alphabets are characterised by their handwriting style of letterforms, which makes the text look elegant and decorative. Copy cursive uppercase and lowercase alphabets and use them in names, headings or add combining characters to it.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.8]">Letters included in the <a href="https://aestheticfonts.in/blog/what-is-unicode-font/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">Unicode</a> Mathematical Script alphabet are 𝒜, ℬ, 𝒞 etc. and also lowercase 𝒶, 𝒷, 𝒸 etc. There is also bold script that has thick strokes, and light script which looks more fancy.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Alphabets to copy -->
    <section class="mb-12 grid gap-4">
      <div class="card px-5 py-4">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Write Capital Letters in Cursive (A-Z)</h3>
        <p class="text-[1.5rem] leading-[1.6] break-all select-all" dir="ltr">𝓐𝓑𝓒𝓓𝓔𝓕𝓖𝓗𝓘𝓙𝓚𝓛𝓜𝓝𝓞𝓟𝓠𝓡𝓢𝓣𝓤𝓥𝓦𝓧𝓨𝓩</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card px-5 py-4">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Small Cursive Letters (a-z)</h3>
        <p class="text-[1.5rem] leading-[1.6] break-all select-all" dir="ltr">𝓪𝓫𝓬𝓭𝓮𝓯𝓰𝓱𝓲𝓳𝓴𝓵𝓶𝓷𝓸𝓹𝓺𝓻𝓼𝓽𝓾𝓿𝔀𝔁𝔂𝔃</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What is -->
    <section class="mb-12 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">What Is Cursive Font?</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">Cursive fonts are a special style of typefaces which are similar to handwriting, where the letters are joined together with cursive lines. Lettering can be inspired by regular handwriting, calligraphy or any other casual style of handwriting.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8]">Cursive <a href="https://aestheticfonts.in/blog/how-to-create-your-own-font/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">fonts</a> are categorized into styles including formal script, casual script, brush lettering and ornate handwriting. They all are equal in strokes, connections and decorations.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- How to use -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">How to Use Cursive Text Online</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-5"><a href="https://aestheticfonts.in/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">This Font Generator</a> replaces simple text with a script font that displays in the Unicode character set. Simply type a name, word, caption, or short phrase and choose from a set of styles to find one that appeals to you without having to download a new font.</p>
      <ol class="list-none p-0 m-0 flex flex-col gap-3 mb-5">
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7] flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-primary">1.</span> <span><strong class="font-semibold">Input your text:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Type a name, word, caption, or phrase into the field.</span></span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7] flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-primary">2.</span> <span><strong class="font-semibold">Pick a cursive style:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Try light script, bold script, or any other style that fits.</span></span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7] flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-primary">3.</span> <span><strong class="font-semibold">Copy your text:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Click the Copy button next to the chosen version of text.</span></span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7] flex gap-3"><span class="font-semibold text-primary">4.</span> <span><strong class="font-semibold">Paste your text:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Use copied Unicode symbols in social media bios, messages, captions, etc.</span></span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8]">The transformation can even be done in the browser by simply mapping characters. Since the output is all font characters, you can just copy and paste it without the need for downloading a font file.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Handwriting vs Unicode -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Is Cursive Unicode Text the Same as Handwriting?</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">No. Cursive Unicode text and a real handwriting font are two different things. The former is made using specific Unicode characters, while the latter is written on a writing surface with a pen.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">The Unicode Standard includes code points for Mathematical Script and Mathematical Bold Script characters in the Mathematical Alphanumeric Symbols range. These characters are intended for mathematical notation but are sometimes used to render fancy text.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8]">A single Unicode character does not contain the whole sequence of connected letter strokes. It does not automatically link neighbouring characters the way cursive writing or a cursive font face does.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Best script fonts -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Which Is the Best Font for Script-Style, Flowing Writing?</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-5">Curved lines, embellished shapes and handwritten letterforms appear in many different styles of typography. How they look depends on the style of each letter, the writing tool it imitates, and the degree of connectedness.</p>
      <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 flex flex-col gap-3 mb-5">
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Calligraphy:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Uses deliberate strokes with raised and fancy details.</span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Brush:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Mimics writing with a broad-tipped tool, usually with flowing strokes.</span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Formal Script:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Elegant, flowing, connected letterforms, such as you might see on a wedding invitation.</span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Casual:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Similar to everyday handwriting but with simplified strokes.</span></li>
        <li class="card px-5 py-3.5 text-sm leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold"><a href="https://aestheticfonts.in/italic/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">Italic</a>:</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">A style that slants the letterforms, but not necessarily to the degree of a cursive letter.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8]">These fonts come as standard in graphic design software, and certain Unicode text generators allow some of these styles to be copied and pasted directly into text fields.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Instagram / LinkedIn -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Can You Use Cursive on Instagram or LinkedIn?</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">Yes, Unicode cursive letters are supported in <a href="https://aestheticfonts.in/blog/instagram-bio-for-boys/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">Instagram</a> and LinkedIn text areas. They can be used for display names, profile bios and short descriptions.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">Support depends on the field. Display names and page descriptions generally accept symbols, but areas like account handles, search boxes and other submittable fields may limit input to plain letters and numbers.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8]">Regular text is easier for readers to read and search on LinkedIn, so keep professional summaries and experience in plain text. Use cursive lettering sparingly for short, decorative text.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Misaligned / boxes -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Why Are Some of My Cursive Characters Misaligned or Appearing as Boxes?</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">Some characters may look misaligned when the Unicode characters come from different character blocks. For example, your device may use one font for most of the script letters and another for the characters it does not support, which can change the stroke thickness or shape.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8] mb-3">Certain light Mathematical Script characters, ℬ, ℰ, ℱ, ℋ, ℐ, ℒ, ℳ, ℛ, ℯ, ℊ, ℴ, are also characters in the Letterlike Symbols block and are not part of the main Mathematical Alphanumeric Symbols range. They may look different from neighbouring characters.</p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-[1.8]">The <a href="https://aestheticfonts.in/blog/unicode-empty-boxes/" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2 hover:no-underline">square box, missing-glyph box or "tofu" character</a> is displayed when a character is not present in the font used by the application. The app receiving the text must also support the character.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</CursivePage>
